---
import { url } from "../lib/docs";
---

<figure class="demo-player">
  <video
    controls
    playsinline
    preload="none"
    poster={url("demos/duckpad-overview.jpg")}
    width="1920"
    height="1080"
    aria-label="Duckpad in one minute: build visual pipelines, explore results and version your work"
    aria-describedby="product-video-caption"
  >
    <source src={url("demos/duckpad-overview.mp4")} type="video/mp4" />
    <track
      kind="captions"
      src={url("demos/duckpad-overview.vtt")}
      srclang="en"
      label="English"
      default
    />
    Your browser cannot play this video.{" "}
    <a href={url("demos/duckpad-overview.mp4")}>
      Download the one-minute video.
    </a>
  </video>
  <figcaption id="product-video-caption">
    <span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Duckpad in one minute ·
    English narration · Real app footage, edited for pace{" "}
    <a href={url("docs/quickstart/")}>Build your first pipeline ↗</a>
  </figcaption>
  <details class="video-transcript">
    <summary>Read the video transcript</summary>
    <div>
      <p>
        Your next pipeline starts with a drag. Meet Duckpad. An open-source
        workspace for people who work with data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Drop a step onto the canvas. Connect your sources. Shape the flow. Use
        simple controls to filter, join, and transform. Or open the SQL when you
        want to go deeper.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>On screen:</em> A Filter node is dragged into the Northstar
        pipeline, connected to Orders, and configured to keep amounts greater
        than 100. The Code workspace shows the SQL behind a transformation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Run with DuckDB, then explore the result right where you built it.
        Wonder where a number came from? Click it. Follow the calculation, all
        the way back to the source. Turn useful steps into reusable components.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>On screen:</em> The Regional revenue report shows a value of 7,131.
        Clicking it opens a lineage graph with its 27 contributing source
        values. A nested component reveals the filter and aggregation it
        contains.
      </p>
      <p>
        And keep your work versioned with Git. Review what changed. Explore a
        branch. Build with the confidence to go back. From the first connection
        to a result you can explain. Duckpad. See the flow. Trust the result.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>On screen:</em> Git history and version comparison lead into
        creating an independent working branch. The film closes with “Build your
        first pipeline.”
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>
</figure>

<style>
  .video-transcript {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 15px 18px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .video-transcript > div {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin: 18px auto 0;
  }
  .video-transcript p + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
</style>
